new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..49257bde48c2cb068ab03315e236c9669fe1e2f4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/games/totk/docs/mod-support.md
@@ -0,0 +1,167 @@
+# RomFS Mod Support
+
+This project now supports loading additional code modules (mods) from the RomFS at runtime.
+
+## How It Works
+
+Mods are loaded as additional NSO modules (like `subsdk9`) from a `mods/` directory in your extracted RomFS. The loader reads a `patches.json` manifest that lists which modules to load.
+
+## Setup
+
+### 1. Prepare Your Mod Files
+
+Extract your mod's binary files into the RomFS structure:
+
+```
+extracted/v143/romfs/
+├── mods/
+│   ├── patches.json          # Manifest file
+│   ├── subsdk9.patched.bin   # Your mod binary
+│   └── another_mod.patched.bin
+├── ... (other RomFS files)
+```
+
+### 2. Create patches.json
+
+Create a `patches.json` file listing the modules to load:
+
+```json
+{
+  "modules": [
+    "subsdk9",
+    "another_mod"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### 3. Rebuild the App
+
+After adding mods, rebuild your app:
+
+```bash
+python3.14 build_app.py ~/Games/totk.xci -k ~/keys/prod.keys
+```
+
+The build will include the mods in the RomFS overlay.
+
+## Technical Details
+
+### Module Format
+
+Each mod must be a valid ARM64 NSO module with:
+- MOD0 header
+- Dynamic section with symbol tables
+- Properly relocated code (use `patch_nso.py` to prepare)
+
+### Loading Order
+
+1. Base modules (`main`, `subsdk0`, `sdk`) are loaded first
+2. Mod modules are loaded from `mods/patches.json`
+3. All modules share the same symbol resolution namespace
+
+### Limitations
+
+- Maximum 8 additional mod modules
+- Mods cannot override base module symbols
+- Mods must be compatible with the game version
+
+## Example: TOTK-Telemetry Mod
+
+To use the TOTK-Telemetry mod:
+
+1. Extract `TOTK-Telemetry.zip`
+2. Copy `exefs/subsdk9` to `extracted/v143/romfs/mods/subsdk9.patched.bin`
+3. Create `extracted/v143/romfs/mods/patches.json`:
+   ```json
+   {
+     "modules": ["subsdk9"]
+   }
+   ```
+4. Rebuild the app
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Mod Not Loading
+
+Check the log at `~/Library/Logs/MacNativeGames/totk.log`:
+
+- `[totk] loading RomFS mods from ...` - Loader found patches.json
+- `[totk] loaded mod subsdk9 at ...` - Module loaded successfully
+- `[totk] mod subsdk9 not found at ...` - File missing
+- `[totk] mod subsdk9 missing MOD0 header` - Invalid module format
+
+### Game Crashes
+
+If the game crashes after loading a mod:
+
+1. Check if the mod is compiled for the correct architecture (ARM64)
+2. Verify the mod is compatible with your game version
+3. Try removing the mod and rebuilding to confirm it's the cause
+4. Check `totk.log` for error messages
+
+## Advanced: Multiple Mods
+
+You can load multiple mods simultaneously:
+
+```json
+{
+  "modules": [
+    "telemetry",
+    "performance_monitor",
+    "debug_overlay"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Make sure mods don't conflict with each other (e.g., hooking the same functions).
+
+## Development Notes
+
+### Preparing Mod Binaries
+
+Use the project's existing toolchain to prepare mod binaries:
+
+```bash
+# Patch an NSO file for macOS
+python3 games/totk/third_party/d2r/patch_nso.py \
+  path/to/subsdk9 \
+  output_dir \
+  subsdk9
+```
+
+This creates a `subsdk9.patched.bin` file ready for loading.
+
+### Symbol Resolution
+
+Mods can:
+- Call functions from base modules (resolved automatically)
+- Export new functions for other mods to use
+- Override weak symbols from base modules
+
+Mods cannot:
+- Override strong symbols from base modules
+- Modify base module code at runtime
+
+## Future Enhancements
+
+Potential improvements:
+- Hot-reload mods without restarting
+- Mod dependency resolution
+- Version compatibility checks
+- Automatic patch application
+
+## Security Considerations
+
+⚠️ **Warning**: Mods run with the same privileges as the game. Only use mods from trusted sources.
+
+The loader validates:
+- File existence and readability
+- MOD0 header presence
+- Basic file format
+
+It does NOT validate:
+- Code correctness
+- Malicious behavior
+- Compatibility beyond basic format
+
+Always backup your saves before using mods!
